From b81152a9765dfabe18664eaf68a5d4897405aa78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:09:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Add PCI seL4 backend, fix device listing, add driver
 guide

- BOOT/SEL4: PCI config backend (mechanism #1) with an injected port-I/O layer,
  plus the seL4 binding that issues an I/O-port cap for 0xCF8-0xCFF.
- initial_task installs the backend after Core startup and lists devices.
- Device registry: classify USB host/bridge/audio/wireless correctly (USB host
  was reported as an input device), read subsystem IDs and MSI/MSI-X/PCIe
  capability offsets (bounded walk), keep device_id and driver binding across
  rescans, raise capacities to 256 devices / 64 drivers.
- Remove the two unbuilt printf-based PCI scanner prototypes.
- Host tests for all of the above (make test-boot).
- Rewrite DRIVER_DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md and DEVICE_DRIVER_STATUS.md to match the
  code; open-source-first driver policy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
